  "query_preview": "..(This Afternoon Through Thursday)\nIssued at 1153 AM MST Fri Nov 6 2026\n\nMean western NOAM ridging will support mild and dry weather as \nPac flow continues aloft. Weak/skirting impulses will support cool\nfronts at times to knock temps down a few degrees. Temps will be \nabove normal in the period with the warmest days being this \nweekend, particularity Sunday when highs will average 20 degrees \nabove normal. Areas of fog can be expected toward south central SD\ntonight. Any fog will quickly burn off Saturday morning with \ntemps recovering nicely by afternoon. Breezy NW winds will develop\nSat ahead of the next impulse moving across southern Canada, with\na few gusts approaching 35 to 40 mph near the ND border. \nOtherwise, mild Saturday with highs in the 60s. Another stronger \ntrough will take a similar path across southern Canada on Sunday, \nwith warm conditions expected across the FA ahead of the system as\nhighs reach in the 60s and 70s. Breezy south winds can also be \nexpected, supporting elevated fire weather conds across parts of \nthe area. Cool front will move through Sunday night. This will \nknock temps back down into the 50s and 60s for Monday. Zonal/mild \nPac flow expected through next week, with mild and dry weather \ncontinuing, as periodic cool fronts move through.",
